  "texto": "# Arriving\n@energy 2\n> Speak slowly, as if the listener were already half asleep.\n\n[slow][soft]Find a comfortable position and let your body grow heavy.\nLet the chair or the bed hold all of your weight.\nClose your eyes whenever you're ready.\n[breathe]\nBreathe in through your nose, deep and unhurried.\nExhale through your mouth, like a wave pulling back from the shore.\n[breathe]\nNotice your shoulders, your jaw and your hands.\nLet each one soften a little more.\nCan you feel your body starting to slow down? [up]\nThere's nothing to do but be here.[/soft][/slow]\n[pause 3s]\n\n# The surface\n@energy 2\n> Paint the scene gently. No rush.\n\n[soft]Now imagine you're floating on a calm sea.\nThe water is warm, and the sky is pale blue with a few white clouds.\nSmall waves rise and fall beneath your back, like a slow breath.\n[breathe]\nCan you feel the sun resting on your face? [up]\nFar away, a seagull calls, and then everything is silent again.\nThere's nothing to fix and nowhere to be.\n[breathe]\nJust the gentle rocking of the water, again and again.\nEach wave carries away a little of the day's **tiredness**.\nAnd you keep floating, calm and at ease.[/soft]\n[pause 3s]\n\n# Sinking down\n@energy 1\n> Even slower now. Let the words sink with the listener.\n\n[slow][soft]Now let yourself sink, very gently, below the surface.\nThe light turns green, then deep blue, then softer still.\n[breathe]\nWith every breath, you drift a little deeper.\nTen meters, twenty meters… the noise of the world stays above.\nDown here you can breathe with ease, like in a dream.\n[breathe]\nFar ahead, a whale passes by, singing a long, low song.\nIts voice fills the water and reaches your chest.\nListen without thinking about anything.[/soft][/slow]\n[pause 3s]\n\n# The quiet deep\n@energy 1\n> Almost a whisper, but every word clear.\n\n[soft]Here, at the bottom of the ocean, everything is still.\nTiny lights glow around you, like stars in a dark sky.\nA glass-like jellyfish drifts past, shining violet.\n[breathe]\nYou are safe and calm; the water holds you.\nOver the sand and the stones, everything rests.\nIf a thought comes, let it rise like a bubble.\nWatch it float toward the surface, without following it.\n[breathe]\nWhat remains when the thoughts are gone? [up]\nOnly your breathing, slow and deep.\nStay here a moment longer.[/soft]\n[pause 3s]\n\n# Returning\n@energy 2\n> Gently bring the listener back. A warmer tone at the end.\n\n[slow]Now, little by little, begin to rise toward the light.\nFeel the water grow warmer and clearer around you.[/slow]\n[breathe]\nTake one deep breath and let it fill your whole chest.\nWiggle your fingers and your toes.\nNotice the surface beneath your body and the air in the room.\n[breathe]\nWhen you're ready, open your eyes.\nCarry this calm with you, like a small treasure from the deep.\nCome back to it whenever you need it. [down]\n[pause 3s]\n"
